    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> export default function highlight\r\n\r\nThere is a benefit in having both function namely exported: it explicitly state what are each functions. Also there is not real hierarchy between them. So I would stay like that, especially because this is not an API to be used outside of the library.\r\n\r\n> only test highlight()\r\n\r\nHaving two functions allows for finer grained tests and makes responsibility of each functions  more explicit. If tests on `parseHighlightedAttribute` do not fail but tests on `parseAlgoliaHit` fail, we know that the error is on `parseAlgoliaHit` for sure. Otherwise it means that we have to analyze both functions to know the source of the error.",
    "commit_id": "8c67ff65113466db56cedefd497df6bb823bd949",
